      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m fine to change it to `EnforceLimitSpecInvariants` but how about `EnforceLimitSpecInvariantsOnDeviceLimitsAfterValidation`. The thing I want to know looking at Limits.h/cpp is when is this applied and on what thing.\n\nIn a more type friendly language like F# these would all be different types \n\n`PhysicalAdapterLimits`\n`NormalizedAdapterLimits`\n`RequiredLimits`\n`ReifiedRequiredLimits`\n`ValidatedDeviceLimits`\n`NormalizedDeviceLimits`\n\nThen each function would take one type and return the next.\n\n    NormalizedAdapterLimits NormalizeLimits(PhysicalAdapterLimits l)\n\nThen it would be clear what each function is used for because you couldn\u0027t pass anything except `ValidatedDeviceLimits` to this function and it would return `NormalizedDeviceLimits`. But, all these functions just take `Limits` so it\u0027s difficult to tell what\u0027s used for what at a glance. Putting it in the name helps I think but I\u0027m ok with whatever.",
      "parentUuid": "94724e7b_f36aa45a",
      "revId": "41c7266130ac4bf66fd5518a07be72e1e874cae8",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
